---
name: extension-call-in-a-def-body
description: "a single-line `extension (r) def m` is callable from a def body with nothing above it"
backends: [int, jvm, js, v2]
---

# Two conditions, and the case is written to meet both

The declaration below is the **single-line** form and there is **no top-level statement above the
`def`**. Both were required to reproduce, which is why three earlier drafts of this case were green
on v2 and had their `known-red` correctly rejected as stale.

**GREEN ON EVERY BACKEND since 2026-08-14; the `known-red` is gone.** The two conditions describe
one mechanism rather than two: the single-line form has no NL after the receiver `)`, so the member
block was never opened, so the receiver stayed live and **every following `def` was absorbed as an
extension member** — which is why a statement above helped whatever it contained (it ended the run
of absorbable declarations) and why the block form was immune. Fixed in the reference front by
`0428861ff` and in F by `layoutCloseX`; `tests/e2e/single-line-extension-gate.sh` pins the
absorption itself rather than either front's symptom.

| extension form | statement above the def? | call site | v2 before | v2 now |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| single-line | — | top level | ✅ | ✅ |
| single-line | yes, uses the member | def body | ✅ | ✅ |
| single-line | yes, touches no extension | def body | ✅ | ✅ |
| single-line | yes, but BELOW the def | def body | ❌ | ✅ |
| single-line | no | def body | ❌ **this case** | ✅ |
| single-line | no | `def main` directly | ❌ | ✅ |
| block form | no | def body | ✅ | ✅ |
| block form | yes, uses another member | def body | ✅ | ✅ |

int, jvm and js answer in every row. A member *with* a parameter failed identically on the red rows,
so this was not the receiver being miscounted against a member that declares none — which is what the
defect was first, wrongly, filed as.

```scalascript
case class Box(v: String)
extension (s: String) def boxed: Box = Box(s)
def inBody(): Unit = println("body-" + "a".boxed.v)
def main(): Unit = inBody()
```
